      ],
      "source": "https://www.austria.info/en-us/recommendations/discover-austria/stift-klosterneuburg/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The abbey has combined history, art, faith, and wine culture for over 900 years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.stift-klosterneuburg.at/welcome/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Klosterneuburg sits on the Danube, just north of Vienna, separated by the Kahlenberg and Leopoldsberg hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Klosterneuburg",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town hosts Austria’s oldest winery; a guided tour descends into 900‑year‑old monastic cellars.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.austria.info/en-us/recommendations/discover-austria/stift-klosterneuburg/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 2026 a new guided tour will reveal the von Trapp family’s early years in Klosterneuburg before their move to Salzburg.",
